            <ArticleTitle>Behavioral and magnetoencephalographic correlates of plasticity in the adult human brain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10413-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent behavioral and physiological evidence suggests that even brief sensory deprivation can lead to the rapid emergence of new and functionally effective neural connections in the adult human brain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
